@neurograce I notice you also asked about cases where stimuli are hard to synthesize. Some thoughts:

(1) We can try to get good enough about reasoning from first principles on weights to trust our deductive analysis.
(2) We can intervene on circuits (editing weights) instead of input

@neurograce This gives us a really neat experimental loop:
(1) Deductively reason about features based on the weights.
(2) Validate your hypothesis experimentally.

